+# PR Triage Bot — Phase 1 MVP Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Build a Dockerized React + Express app that takes a GitHub PR URL, runs a 3-agent Claude analysis pipeline, and presents a layered review UI (executive summary → change clusters → annotated diffs) with WebSocket streaming.
+
+**Architecture:** Single-container app — Express backend serves the Vite-built React frontend. Backend orchestrates three Claude agents in sequence (file analysis → clustering → ranking), streaming results to the frontend via WebSocket. GitHub API (Octokit) fetches PR diffs. All config via `.env`.
+
+**Tech Stack:** React 18 + TypeScript + Vite (frontend), Node.js + Express + TypeScript (backend), Anthropic TypeScript SDK, Octokit, ws (WebSocket), Docker + Docker Compose, Vitest (testing).
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-02-pr-triage-bot-design.md`
+
+---
+
+## File Structure
+
+```
+pr-triage-bot/
+├── docker-compose.yml              # Single "app" service, PORT_PREFIX parameterized
+├── Dockerfile                      # Multi-stage: build frontend, run backend
+├── .env.example                    # PORT_PREFIX, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GITHUB_TOKEN
+├── .gitignore
+│
+├── backend/
+│   ├── package.json
